# Pig Script
@cooldown 30s

@fast
@using Harha

@define String[] correctStrings = String["One! The loneliest number... just like me down here in this cellar. KEEP GOING!!!", "Two! That's how many eyes I have. I think. It's dark down here.", "Three little pigs! Those are my cousins, actually.", "Four walls in this cellar. I've counted. Many times.", "Five! High five! Oh wait... hooves.", "Six! If you flip it, it's a 9. Blew my mind the first century.", "Seven! Lucky number seven! Not so lucky for a pig in a cellar though.", "Eight looks like a snowman! I miss snowmen.", "Nine! So close to ten I can TASTE it!", "TEN! Double digits baby! Only 990 to go!", "Eleven looks like two little legs. I miss walking outside.", "A dozen! That's how many centuries I've been stuck here!", "Thirteen! Unlucky? My whole LIFE is unlucky, friend.", "Fourteen! A fortnight! I used to love fortnights. Now they all blend together.", "Fifteen! A quarter of the way to sixty! I don't know why I said that!", "Sweet sixteen! I never had a sweet sixteen party. Pigs don't get those.", "Seventeen! That's a prime number. I've had a LOT of time to learn math.", "Eighteen! Old enough to vote! Do pigs vote? I honestly forgot.", "Nineteen! The last teen number! Goodbye teens!", "Twenty! I slept for 20 days once down here! Or was it 20 years?", "Twenty-one! Blackjack! I used to play cards with the fish outside the window.", "Twenty-two! Double twos! Double the fun!", "Twenty-three! Michael Jordan's number! ...who is Michael Jordan?", "Twenty-four hours in a day! Not that time means anything down here.", "Quarter of a hundred! We're cruising now!", "Twenty-six letters in the alphabet! I recite them to stay sane!", "Twenty-seven! That's a perfect cube. 3 times 3 times 3. I do a lot of math.", "Twenty-eight days in February! Usually! Sometimes 29! Isn't that WILD?", "Twenty-nine! A prime number AND it rhymes with fine! Twenty-fine!", "THIRTY! Three percent done! Wait... that sounds less impressive.", "Thirty-one! Like the ice cream place! I would do unspeakable things for ice cream.", "Thirty-two! Freezing point of water in Fahrenheit! This cellar is FREEZING.", "Thirty-three! Double threes! My lucky number! Well, one of many.", "Thirty-four! Nothing super special about 34 but I love it anyway!", "Thirty-five! A nickel and a quarter! I miss money. Do they still use money?", "Thirty-six! A perfect square! Six times six!", "Thirty-seven is my least favorite number... just gives me a weird vibe.", "Thirty-eight! That's better. Much better energy than 37.", "Thirty-nine! One away from forty! The suspense!", "FORTY! We're 4% there! I'm going to cry tears of joy.", "41! Now THAT'S a number with character!", "Forty-two! The answer to life, the universe, and everything! I read that book six hundred years ago!", "43! Do you hear that? Me neither. It's very quiet down here.", "Forty-four! Double fours! Perfectly symmetrical! Like my ears! ...probably.", "45! There's a crack in the ceiling that looks like the number 45. I might be losing it.", "I'm adding 46 to my list of all-time favorites!", "Forty-seven! AK-47! ...I only know that from a book I found floating by the window.", "48! When I get out, I'm eating a feast so big they'll write songs about it!", "49! That's 7 squared! Perfect square! Perfection!", "FIFTY! Five percent! We're actually making PROGRESS!", "Fifty-one! Area 51! Are aliens real? I've been underwater for 1200 years, I have no idea.", "Fifty-two cards in a deck! Fifty-two weeks in a year! What a versatile number!", "53 just hits different when you've been underwater for centuries.", "Bless you for bringing me 54. Bless you.", "Fifty-five! Speed limit on the highway! I miss roads!", "I used to think 56 was just okay. Now I think it's SPECTACULAR.", "57! The floor is slimy today. Well, every day. But today I noticed.", "58! My cellar used to be a wine cellar. All the wine floated away centuries ago.", "59! You're the first person to talk to me in... I don't want to think about how long.", "Sixty! Seconds in a minute! Minutes in an hour! What a workhorse of a number!", "61! A snail can sleep for three years! Amateur. I slept through century four.", "62! I wish I could play this number on a piano. I used to play. With my snout. Badly.", "63! Say it louder for the fish in the back! 63!!!", "Sixty-four! Squares on a chess board! I play chess against a crab sometimes. He cheats.", "Sixty-five! Retirement age! I've been retired for about 1,190 years!", "Sixty-six! Route 66! I always wanted to road trip across America!", "67! I tried meditation. I reached enlightenment around century 8. Then I lost it. Still stuck.", "68! When I'm free, I'm telling everyone about the hero who counted me out of prison.", "Sixty-nine! Hehehe. Nice.", "70! Do they still have sunsets? I bet they're still beautiful.", "71! I've been WAITING for this one!", "Seventy-two! The rule of 72! Compound interest! My financial knowledge is 12 centuries old!", "Seventy-three! Sheldon's favorite number! ...I don't know who Sheldon is but a fish told me.", "74! This is a TEAM effort and we are the BEST team!", "Seventy-five! Three quarters of a hundred! Beautiful!", "76! I just saw a really big fish swim by the window!", "Seventy-seven! Double sevens! Double lucky! Unless you're me!", "78! *taps hooves rhythmically* We've got a rhythm going!", "79! I just squealed a little. Okay a lot.", "Eighty! Eight percent! We are doing this! We are REALLY doing this!", "81! That's 9 squared! Perfect square! Perfection!", "82! I tried to write a novel once. The ink kept dissolving. Classic cellar problems.", "83! I want to frame this number and hang it on my cellar wall!", "84! The vibe in this cellar right now is UNMATCHED!", "85! I'm getting that pre-milestone tingle! You know the one!", "86! What if I forgot what outside looks like? I'll figure it out! Keep counting!", "87! A fish asked me what I was doing. I said counting. It said 'what's counting?' I cried.", "Eighty-eight! Piano keys! I used to play piano with my hooves. Badly.", "89! A jiffy is an actual unit of time! One hundredth of a second!", "Ninety! Almost to a hundred! My heart is POUNDING!", "Ninety-one! Nine more to a hundred! Single digits away! NINE!", "Ninety-two! Eight to go! I can feel it in my TROTTERS!", "Ninety-three! Seven away! The countdown within the countdown!", "Ninety-four! SIX more! I'm pacing around the cellar!", "Ninety-five! FIVE! Just five more to the first hundred!", "Ninety-six! FOUR! My snout is twitching!", "Ninety-seven! THREE! I might faint!", "Ninety-eight! TWO! TWO MORE!", "NINETY-NINE! One more! ONE MORE TO A HUNDRED!", "ONE HUNDRED!!! TEN PERCENT!!! I'm shaking! I'm literally shaking!", "A hundred and one! Like the dalmatians! I love dogs! They don't love me though.", "The seaweed swayed when you said 102. Even nature loves it!", "103! My autobiography title: 'Wet, Dark, and Counting: The John Pork Story.'", "104! The start of a brand new era of numbers!", "105! I made up a song about that number! It goes: '105, 105, beautiful 105!' That's the whole song.", "106! The shortest war in history lasted 38 minutes! I've been imprisoned for 6.3 billion minutes!", "PRIME! 107 is prime! I've memorized all primes up to 10,000. What else is there to do?", "A hundred and eight! Sacred number in Buddhism! I got spiritual around century five.", "109! I once arm-wrestled an eel. We both lost. Don't ask.", "110! The door rattled! Just the current. But a pig can dream.", "One-eleven! All ones! It's like a tiny parade of toothpicks!", "One-twelve! Emergency number in Europe! Not that anyone's calling for ME.", "113! Cows have best friends! I wonder if that fish is MY best friend. Besides you!", "114! That number has a great beat! I'm nodding my head! Oink oink oink!", "115! Seriously though, thank you for doing this. No one else ever visited.", "116! I found a shiny rock earlier. I named it 116. After this number.", "Master Chief's number! ...I think? A crab mentioned it once.", "118! If this were a musical, this would be the part where I do a big dance number!", "119! I bet the moon is still up there. I think about the moon a lot.", "One-twenty! That's a factorial of 5! Math keeps me alive down here!", "121! I'm going to eat SO much corn when I get out. Mountains of corn.", "122! I started a book club with the fish. They have terrible taste in literature.", "One-two-three! Easy as A-B-C! Oh this one sparks joy!", "124! A starfish landed on the window! We made eye contact! All five of them!", "Beautiful, gorgeous, stunning 125!", "126! A seahorse winked at me. Or blinked. Hard to tell with seahorses.", "127! You could be doing anything right now and you're here counting with a pig. You're amazing.", "One twenty-eight! A power of two! Computer science vibes!", "129! You know what sounds good? Literally any food. I've been eating kelp for centuries.", "130! There are more stars in the sky than grains of sand on Earth! A fish told me!", "131! Is counting a skill? I think I'm the world's foremost expert at this point.", "132! If I had a trophy for every number, this one would be gold!", "133! My cellar is about 10 by 10 hooves. I've measured. Many, many times.", "134! A piece of seaweed drifted in through the crack. I'm keeping it as a pet.", "135! Any% freedom run! No glitches! Pure skill!", "136! If counting to 1000 were an Olympic sport, we'd get GOLD!", "137! Most people would have given up by now. You're built different.", "I'm adding 138 to my list of all-time favorites!", "139! We're built different! We don't quit! We COUNT!", "140 makes my little curly tail wiggle with joy!", "141! A palindrome! Same forwards and backwards! Fancy!", "142! A crab challenged me to a dance battle. I lost. Crabs have more legs. Unfair advantage.", "143! Wait, you're still there right? Don't leave! Keep counting!", "One forty-four! A gross! Also twelve squared! Magnificent!", "145! My interior design down here is 'rustic ocean dungeon chic.'", "146! You know what 146 represents? Hope. Every number is hope.", "147! This is the greatest counting session in the history of counting sessions!", "148! Sometimes I blow bubbles and pretend they're words floating up to the surface.", "I whisper 149 to myself sometimes. Is that weird?", "ONE FIFTY! Fifteen percent! We're cookin' now! ...please don't cook me.", "Palindrome alert! 151 looks the same in a mirror!", "152! Bananas are berries but strawberries aren't! The world makes no sense!", "One fifty-three! A narcissistic number! 1 cubed + 5 cubed + 3 cubed = 153! I love narcissistic numbers!", "154! Trees! I wonder if there are still trees! Big tall dry leafy trees!", "155! That number has such good energy!", "156! When I get out, the first thing I'm doing is looking UP.", "157! I applied for a transfer to a LAND cellar. Application is still pending. For 900 years.", "Oh 158, you beautiful number, you!", "159! If 159 were a food, it'd be... actually everything sounds delicious right now.", "160! The energy right now is IMMACULATE!", "161! A palindrome! Same forwards and backwards! Fancy!", "162! Did you know an octopus has three hearts? I've had time to memorize animal facts.", "163! I'm doing zoomies! Cellar zoomies! Very small zoomies!", "164! The lights flickered. There are no lights. I imagined lights AND THEY FLICKERED.", "165! If I ever get out, I'm writing a book. Chapter 165: The Counting.", "166! I just squealed a little. Okay a lot.", "167! I think the water pressure changed. Or I'm just excited.", "168! If excitement were electricity, I could power a CITY right now!", "One sixty-nine! Thirteen squared! Unlucky squared? Or does it cancel out?", "170! Sorry, I panicked for a second. Thought you forgot about me. We're good. We're good.", "171! Read it backwards. Still 171! Palindrome magic!", "172! A fish asked me what I was doing. I said counting. It said 'what's counting?' I cried.", "173! I haven't heard birdsong in twelve centuries. I hope birds still exist.", "174! The algae on the wall spelled something today. I think it said 'help.' Same, algae. Same.", "One seventy-five! We're really moving! Keep going, friend!", "If I could hug a number, I'd hug 176!", "I'm going to name my first meal as a free pig after 177!", "178! I just did a little underwater piggy dance!", "179! Say it again! Say it slower!", "One eighty! A full half-turn in degrees! Things are turning around for me! Get it?", "A barnacle just fell off the wall at 181. I'll take it as a sign!", "182! Something big is approaching and its name is the next hundred!", "183! A piece of bread floated by once. Greatest day of century seven.", "184! That number reminds me of corn somehow. I miss corn.", "185! We're in the red zone! The excitement zone! The OINK zone!", "186! The next hundred is calling our names! Can you hear it?!", "One eighty-seven! California penal code for... never mind. Next number please.", "188! A school of fish just did a lap around the building! Entertainment!", "189! I've been WAITING for this one!", "One-ninety! Ten away from two hundred! Here we go again!", "One-ninety-one! Nine to go! The two-hundred train is COMING!", "One-ninety-two! Eight away! I remember this feeling from last time!", "One-ninety-three! SEVEN! The anticipation is UNBEARABLE!", "One-ninety-four! Six away! My hooves are clattering on the floor!", "One-ninety-five! FIVE! Halfway through the final stretch!", "One-ninety-six! FOUR! Also fourteen squared! But WHO CARES! FOUR AWAY!", "One-ninety-seven! THREE! The air is electric! Well, the water is electric!", "One-ninety-eight! TWO! JUST TWO! HERE IT COMES!", "ONE-NINETY-NINE! ONE AWAY FROM TWO HUNDRED! SAY IT! SAY IT!", "TWO HUNDRED! Twenty percent! A FIFTH of the way! I could cry! I AM crying!", "201! Fresh into a new hundred! Everything feels POSSIBLE!", "202! New hundred, new me! Same cellar though.", "203! Promise me you won't leave before 1000. PROMISE ME.", "204! Do you hear that? Me neither. It's very quiet down here.", "205! Celebrities do ice baths for like 3 minutes. I've been doing one for 12 centuries. Where's MY podcast?", "206! The walls are growing on me. Literally. There's algae.", "207! Another beautiful number in this beautiful sequence!", "208! Wombat poop is cube-shaped! I have a LOT of random knowledge!", "209! I tried to start a podcast but my microphone was a sea sponge. Zero listeners.", "210! Did you know I can hold my breath forever? Perks of being underwater for 1200 years.", "Two-eleven! Primal and beautiful!", "212! Read it backwards. Still 212! Palindrome magic!", "213! Venus is the only planet that spins clockwise! Just like my tail!", "214! There are more stars in the sky than grains of sand on Earth! A fish told me!", "215! The shortest war in history lasted 38 minutes! I've been imprisoned for 6.3 billion minutes!", "The seaweed swayed when you said 216. Even nature loves it!", "217! Another step toward the surface! I can almost smell the air!", "218! Fun fact: I have given names to 347 different barnacles. Rest in peace, Gerald.", "219! I used to hate getting rained on. Now I'd give anything for rain.", "If 220 were a meal, it'd be the finest slop in the land!", "221! A piece of seaweed drifted in through the crack. I'm keeping it as a pet.", "Two-two-two! Triple twos! Like a little drumroll of twos!", "223! The vibe in this cellar right now is UNMATCHED!", "224! I tried meditation. I reached enlightenment around century 8. Then I lost it. Still stuck.", "225! That's 15 squared! Perfect square! Perfection!", "226! Time is a flat circle. Or a wet circle, in my case.", "227! Every number is a gift and I cherish each one!", "228! My therapist is a sea cucumber. He's not great but the rates are unbeatable.", "229! We're in the ZONE! The counting ZONE!", "230 makes my little curly tail wiggle with joy!", "231! A snail can sleep for three years! Amateur. I slept through century four.", "I used to think 232 was just okay. Now I think it's SPECTACULAR.", "233! I made a friend once. It was a lobster. He moved away.", "Two-three-four! A sequence! I love sequences! They give my life ORDER!", "235! This number means we're 235 steps into our journey together. That's beautiful.", "236! You know what separates us from animals? Counting! Wait. I AM an animal.", "237! A seahorse winked at me. Or blinked. Hard to tell with seahorses.", "238! I started a book club with the fish. They have terrible taste in literature.", "239! I once arm-wrestled an eel. We both lost. Don't ask.", "Oh 240, you beautiful number, you!", "241! My cellar is about 10 by 10 hooves. I've measured. Many, many times.", "Two-forty-two! A palindrome! Same forwards and backwards! Like my face! Round both ways!", "243! I applied for a transfer to a LAND cellar. Application is still pending. For 900 years.", "244! Every number is one step closer to sky. Real sky. Not a ceiling.", "245! A crab challenged me to a dance battle. I lost. Crabs have more legs. Unfair advantage.", "246! *taps hooves rhythmically* We've got a rhythm going!", "Twenty-four-seven! That's how long I've been stuck here! ALL DAY EVERY DAY!", "248! Do they still make slop? Top tier cuisine. Don't let anyone tell you otherwise.", "249! Seriously though, thank you for doing this. No one else ever visited.", "TWO FIFTY! A quarter of a thousand! TWENTY-FIVE PERCENT! This is REAL!", "251! I just squealed a little. Okay a lot.", "252! A palindrome! Same forwards and backwards! Fancy!", "253! Has anyone ever told you you're really good at counting? Because you ARE.", "254! When I get out, I'm eating a feast so big they'll write songs about it!", "255! If excitement were electricity, I could power a CITY right now!", "Two-fifty-six! Two to the eighth power! A byte! A beautiful byte!", "257! Prime and proud! Can't be divided! Won't be divided!", "258! The energy right now is IMMACULATE!", "259! This is the greatest counting session in the history of counting sessions!", "260! I just saw a really big fish swim by the window!", "If I could hug a number, I'd hug 261!", "Palindrome alert! 262 looks the same in a mirror!", "263! A prime number! Only divisible by 1 and itself! Independent, like me!", "Magnificent 264! Simply magnificent!", "265! You could be doing anything right now and you're here counting with a pig. You're amazing.", "266! Wait, you're still there right? Don't leave! Keep counting!", "Keep going! 267 is a wonderful milestone!", "268! What if I forgot what outside looks like? I'll figure it out! Keep counting!", "269! The pressure down here makes everything sound funny. Including numbers!", "270! Sloths can hold their breath for 40 minutes! I can do it for 12 centuries! Beat THAT!", "271! The algae on the wall spelled something today. I think it said 'help.' Same, algae. Same.", "272! Read it backwards. Still 272! Palindrome magic!", "273! Is counting a skill? I think I'm the world's foremost expert at this point.", "274! I'm going to eat SO much corn when I get out. Mountains of corn.", "275! Personal best pace! Not that I've done this before! But STILL!", "A crab once told me 276 was overrated. That crab was WRONG.", "277! A prime number! Only divisible by 1 and itself! Independent, like me!", "278! I'm doing zoomies! Cellar zoomies! Very small zoomies!", "279! That number could light up this whole dark cellar!", "280! Say it again! Say it slower!", "281! I wonder if I'm famous up there. 'The Legendary Cellar Pig.' Probably not.", "Palindrome alert! 282 looks the same in a mirror!", "283! A jiffy is an actual unit of time! One hundredth of a second!", "284! We're in the approach zone! Fasten your seatbelts!", "285! The door rattled! Just the current. But a pig can dream.", "286! If this were a musical, this would be the part where I do a big dance number!", "287! Every philosopher asks 'why are we here?' I know why I'M here. To count. With you.", "288! Getting closer to the next hundred! The energy is BUILDING!", "289! Cows have best friends! I wonder if that fish is MY best friend. Besides you!", "Two-ninety! Ten to go! Oh no, here comes the suspense again!", "Two-ninety-one! Nine! My pulse is rising! Do pigs have pulses? YES!", "Two-ninety-two! Eight! Also a palindrome! But I'm too excited to care!", "Two-ninety-three! SEVEN! Every number is a heartbeat now!", "Two-ninety-four! SIX! The walls are vibrating! That might be me vibrating!", "Two-ninety-five! FIVE AWAY! I swear the water just got warmer!", "Two-ninety-six! FOUR! The barnacles are cheering! In my imagination!", "Two-ninety-seven! THREE! I can almost SEE the three in the three hundred!", "Two-ninety-eight! TWO! My tail is spinning like a propeller!", "TWO-NINETY-NINE! ONE! JUST ONE! GIVE IT TO ME!", "THREE HUNDRED!!! THIRTY PERCENT!!! We're in the 300s! I never dreamed this day would come!", "301! I think the water pressure changed. Or I'm just excited.", "302! This is better than Christmas! Not that I've had Christmas in 1200 years!", "Palindrome alert! 303 looks the same in a mirror!", "304! That number has a great beat! I'm nodding my head! Oink oink oink!", "305! Say it louder for the fish in the back! 305!!!", "306! Every number brings me closer to freedom!", "307! Most people would have given up by now. You're built different.", "Glorious 308! Absolutely glorious!", "309! I tried to start a podcast but my microphone was a sea sponge. Zero listeners.", "Splendid! 310 is absolutely splendid!", "311! I tried to write a novel once. The ink kept dissolving. Classic cellar problems.", "312! My hooves are pruney. Have been for about 600 years.", "Palindrome alert! 313 looks the same in a mirror!", "Three-fourteen! Like pi! 3.14! I love pi! Not pie though. Well, also pie. I love pie too.", "315! If counting to 1000 were an Olympic sport, we'd get GOLD!", "316! I made a friend once. It was a lobster. He moved away.", "317! A jellyfish just floated by! Hi jellyfish! We're counting!", "318! I've composed 46 symphonies in my head. They all sound like bubbling.", "319! Now THAT'S a number with character!", "320! When I get out I'm going to just... stand somewhere dry. For HOURS.", "Three-two-one! BLAST OFF! We're launching into the mid-hundreds!", "322! A piece of seaweed drifted in through the crack. I'm keeping it as a pet.", "323! Read it backwards. Still 323! Palindrome magic!", "324! I've had a long time to think about the meaning of life. It's numbers. It's always been numbers.", "325! I found a shiny rock earlier. I named it 325. After this number.", "326! I tried counting barnacles once but I lost track at like 50.", "327! I promise I'll never complain about anything ever again once I'm free. Okay maybe a little.", "328! I haven't heard birdsong in twelve centuries. I hope birds still exist.", "329! A school of fish just did a lap around the building! Entertainment!", "330! There's a crack in the ceiling that looks like the number 330. I might be losing it.", "PRIME! 331 is prime! I've memorized all primes up to 10,000. What else is there to do?", "332! Do they still have sunsets? I bet they're still beautiful.", "Triple threes! It's giving angel numbers! The fish say that means something!", "334! Bananas are berries but strawberries aren't! The world makes no sense!", "335! My excitement level is at an all-time high! And it keeps going HIGHER!", "336! I started a book club with the fish. They have terrible taste in literature.", "337! The vibe in this cellar right now is UNMATCHED!", "338! Wind. I miss wind. Even cold wind. ESPECIALLY cold wind.", "Bless you for bringing me 339. Bless you.", "I've been thinking about 340 for YEARS and it lived up to the hype!", "341! I swear that octopus has been watching me for three centuries.", "342! Has anyone ever told you you're really good at counting? Because you ARE.", "343! Read it backwards. Still 343! Palindrome magic!", "344! My dream is to lay in a sunny spot and just... be warm. That's it. That's the dream.", "Three-four-five! A Pythagorean triple! 3 squared plus 4 squared equals 5 squared! MATH!", "346! A piece of bread floated by once. Greatest day of century seven.", "347! My morning routine: wake up, realize I'm still in a cellar, count things. Productive!", "348! The lights flickered. There are no lights. I imagined lights AND THEY FLICKERED.", "349! My interior design down here is 'rustic ocean dungeon chic.'", "Three-fifty! 35 percent! We are CRUSHING this!", "351! I used to think I'd be alone forever. Then you showed up. With NUMBERS.", "352! The walls are growing on me. Literally. There's algae.", "353! Read it backwards. Still 353! Palindrome magic!", "354! My autobiography title: 'Wet, Dark, and Counting: The John Pork Story.'", "355! Pigeons can do math! So can pigs! We're very smart! I'm proof!", "356! A weird shadow just moved. Probably just a fish. Definitely just a fish. ...right?", "357! I'm going to eat SO much corn when I get out. Mountains of corn.", "358! A jiffy is an actual unit of time! One hundredth of a second!", "359! If 359 were a food, it'd be... actually everything sounds delicious right now.", "Three-sixty! Full circle, baby! No scope!", "361! 19 times 19! A perfect square! I love those!", "362! I bet the moon is still up there. I think about the moon a lot.", "363! Read it backwards. Still 363! Palindrome magic!", "364! I think I heard thunder up above! Or a whale. Hard to tell.", "Three-sixty-five! Days in a year! I've seen 438,000 of those!", "366! My fitness routine: pace left, pace right, pace left, pace right. Peak performance.", "367! I once arm-wrestled an eel. We both lost. Don't ask.", "368! There's a species of jellyfish that's immortal! I might be too at this point!", "369! Sometimes I sing numbers to myself. This one's got a nice ring to it!", "370! I heard a creak. Probably just the cellar settling. It's been settling for 1200 years.", "371! You could be doing anything right now and you're here counting with a pig. You're amazing.", "372! I wonder if the farm is still there. Probably not. It's been 1200 years.", "373! Read it backwards. Still 373! Palindrome magic!", "374! There are more stars in the sky than grains of sand on Earth! A fish told me!", "375! Do flowers still smell nice? Please tell me flowers still exist.", "376! You know what 376 represents? Hope. Every number is hope.", "377! My therapist is a sea cucumber. He's not great but the rates are unbeatable.", "378! Venus is the only planet that spins clockwise! Just like my tail!", "379! Before you came along, I was just a pig in a cellar. Now I'm a pig in a cellar WITH PURPOSE.", "380! When I get out, I'm eating a feast so big they'll write songs about it!", "381! I can sense the next milestone approaching! My snout never lies!", "382! The next hundred is calling our names! Can you hear it?!", "383! A palindrome! Same forwards and backwards! Fancy!", "384! Honey never expires! I learned that from a scroll that floated by in century three!", "385! You know what sounds good? Literally any food. I've been eating kelp for centuries.", "386! Do numbers exist if no one says them? I've had 1200 years to ponder this.", "Glorious 387! Absolutely glorious!", "388! I've been WAITING for this one!", "If 389 were a meal, it'd be the finest slop in the land!", "Three-ninety! Here it comes! Ten away from FOUR HUNDRED!", "Three-ninety-one! Nine to go! My heart knows the rhythm by now!", "Three-ninety-two! Eight! I'm doing that thing where I pace in circles!", "Three-ninety-three! SEVEN! The cellar feels SMALLER! In a good way!", "Three-ninety-four! SIX! I can feel four hundred in my BONES!", "Three-ninety-five! FIVE! We've done this climb before and it NEVER gets old!", "Three-ninety-six! FOUR! The fish are gathering at the window!", "Three-ninety-seven! THREE! I'm squealing! Full pig squeal!", "Three-ninety-eight! TWO! The water is BUBBLING around me!", "THREE-NINETY-NINE! ONE! ONE MORE TO FOUR HUNDRED! HERE WE GOOO!", "FOUR HUNDRED! FORTY PERCENT! We're approaching the halfway point! I can SEE it!", "401! We're climbing! Higher and higher! Figuratively! I'm still very deep underwater!", "402! We're on a ROLL! A bread roll! I miss bread!", "403! Time is a flat circle. Or a wet circle, in my case.", "Four-oh-four! Page not found! ...what's a page? What's the internet?", "405! You're the first person to talk to me in... I don't want to think about how long.", "406! Wait, you're still there right? Don't leave! Keep counting!", "407! I had a dream about running through a field. Woke up to fish staring at me.", "408! We're built different! We don't quit! We COUNT!", "409! Please don't stop. I've been alone so long. Just... keep going. Please.", "410! I'm doing zoomies! Cellar zoomies! Very small zoomies!", "411! I've been marinating for 1200 years. I probably taste INCREDIBLE. Please don't eat me.", "412! We're in the ZONE! The counting ZONE!", "413! I tried meditation. I reached enlightenment around century 8. Then I lost it. Still stuck.", "414! I've had approximately 4.3 million naps down here. Still tired.", "415! Personal best pace! Not that I've done this before! But STILL!", "416! A piece of seaweed drifted in through the crack. I'm keeping it as a pet.", "417! Cows have best friends! I wonder if that fish is MY best friend. Besides you!", "418! I wonder what grass feels like. I've almost forgotten.", "419! Full speed ahead! Or, full speed... standing still in a cellar! But SPIRITUALLY ahead!", "Four-twenty! Blaze it! ...is what the seaweed outside my window would say.", "421! The algae on the wall spelled something today. I think it said 'help.' Same, algae. Same.", "422! I wonder if I'm famous up there. 'The Legendary Cellar Pig.' Probably not.", "423! Every number is a gift and I cherish each one!", "Palindrome alert! 424 looks the same in a mirror!", "425! When I get out I'm going to just... stand somewhere dry. For HOURS.", "426! If excitement were electricity, I could power a CITY right now!", "I'm going to name my first meal as a free pig after 427!", "I'm adding 428 to 