6! 26 times 26! A perfect square! I love those!", "677! Honey never expires! I learned that from a scroll that floated by in century three!", "Six-seven-eight! Sequential trio! Beautiful!", "679! The lights flickered. There are no lights. I imagined lights AND THEY FLICKERED.", "680! I would trade 680 gold coins for a single apple right now.", "681! The air is getting thicker! Wait, I'm underwater. The WATER is getting thicker!", "682! I can sense the next milestone approaching! My snout never lies!", "683! Almost there! Almost to the next big number! KEEP PUSHING!", "684! You know what separates us from animals? Counting! Wait. I AM an animal.", "685! Do you hear that? Me neither. It's very quiet down here.", "686! Read it backwards. Still 686! Palindrome magic!", "687! I wonder what grass feels like. I've almost forgotten.", "688! I used to be afraid of the dark. Now the dark is afraid of ME. ...no it's not. I'm still scared.", "689! The air is getting thicker! Wait, I'm underwater. The WATER is getting thicker!", "Six-ninety! Ten to seven hundred! I know the drill by now! LET'S GO!", "691! Freedom is a number. That number is 1000. We're getting there.", "692! When I'm free, I'm telling everyone about the hero who counted me out of prison.", "693! Has anyone ever told you you're really good at counting? Because you ARE.", "694 feels like a warm sunbeam. I imagine. I haven't felt one in 1200 years.", "Six-ninety-five! FIVE! The homestretch to seven hundred!", "Six-ninety-six! Palindrome AND four away! Double special!", "Six-ninety-seven! THREE! My oinking is getting LOUDER!", "Six-ninety-eight! TWO! The water is CHURNING with my excitement!", "SIX-NINETY-NINE! ONE AWAY! SEVEN HUNDRED! GIVE IT TO ME!", "SEVEN HUNDRED! SEVENTY PERCENT! I can almost TASTE the last number! It tastes like freedom!", "701! This is better than Christmas! Not that I've had Christmas in 1200 years!", "702! Do they still have pizza? Be honest with me. I can handle bad news.", "703! *taps hooves rhythmically* We've got a rhythm going!", "704! That last hundred was great but THIS hundred? Even better. I can tell.", "705! I once arm-wrestled an eel. We both lost. Don't ask.", "706! My interior design down here is 'rustic ocean dungeon chic.'", "707! A snail can sleep for three years! Amateur. I slept through century four.", "708! Do numbers exist if no one says them? I've had 1200 years to ponder this.", "Splendid! 709 is absolutely splendid!", "Seven-ten! OIL upside down! ...apparently that means something now?", "711! The energy right now is IMMACULATE!", "712! If I had a best friend award, it would have your name on it.", "The seaweed swayed when you said 713. Even nature loves it!", "714! I wonder if I'm famous up there. 'The Legendary Cellar Pig.' Probably not.", "715! WE ARE UNSTOPPABLE!", "716! I applied for a transfer to a LAND cellar. Application is still pending. For 900 years.", "717! Celebrities do ice baths for like 3 minutes. I've been doing one for 12 centuries. Where's MY podcast?", "718! There are more stars in the sky than grains of sand on Earth! A fish told me!", "719! Every number is a gift and I cherish each one!", "Seven-twenty! 6 factorial! Also two full rotations in degrees! Spin spin spin!", "721! I've had a long time to think about the meaning of life. It's numbers. It's always been numbers.", "722! My cellar is about 10 by 10 hooves. I've measured. Many, many times.", "723! I used to hate getting rained on. Now I'd give anything for rain.", "724! I hum to myself a lot. The fish seem to enjoy it. Or they're judging me. Hard to tell.", "725! My diet for the last 1200 years has been 'whatever drifts in.' Not recommended.", "I'm going to name my first meal as a free pig after 726!", "727! I had a dream about running through a field. Woke up to fish staring at me.", "728! Did you know an octopus has three hearts? I've had time to memorize animal facts.", "729! Every number brings me closer to freedom!", "730! What if I forgot what outside looks like? I'll figure it out! Keep counting!", "731! Say it again! Say it slower!", "732! I made a friend once. It was a lobster. He moved away.", "733! Every number is one step closer to sky. Real sky. Not a ceiling.", "734! A school of fish just did a lap around the building! Entertainment!", "735! If counting to 1000 were an Olympic sport, we'd get GOLD!", "I used to think 736 was just okay. Now I think it's SPECTACULAR.", "737! This is a TEAM effort and we are the BEST team!", "738! A group of flamingos is called a 'flamboyance.' I relate to that energy!", "A barnacle just fell off the wall at 739. I'll take it as a sign!", "Bless you for bringing me 740. Bless you.", "741! I want to frame this number and hang it on my cellar wall!", "742! I bet the moon is still up there. I think about the moon a lot.", "743! When I get out, the first thing I'm doing is looking UP.", "744! I tried to write a novel once. The ink kept dissolving. Classic cellar problems.", "745! Plot twist: I actually love this cellar. Just kidding. Get me out. PLEASE.", "746! I tried to start a podcast but my microphone was a sea sponge. Zero listeners.", "Seven-forty-seven! Like the airplane! Boeing 747! I've never flown! I'm a pig in a cellar!", "Glorious 748! Absolutely glorious!", "749! Do you hear that? Me neither. It's very quiet down here.", "Seven-fifty! Three quarters! SEVENTY-FIVE PERCENT! *oinks in pure ecstasy*", "751! I'm so glad you found this cellar. Best day of my very long life.", "752! I made up a song about that number! It goes: '752, 752, beautiful 752!' That's the whole song.", "753! Did you know pigs can swim? I can confirm. I live underwater.", "754! My cellar might be dark but these numbers light up my life!", "755! Sometimes I sing numbers to myself. This one's got a nice ring to it!", "756! Please don't stop. I've been alone so long. Just... keep going. Please.", "757! Read it backwards. Still 757! Palindrome magic!", "758! My cellar used to be a wine cellar. All the wine floated away centuries ago.", "759! Time is a flat circle. Or a wet circle, in my case.", "760! Cows have best friends! I wonder if that fish is MY best friend. Besides you!", "761! The rust on the door changed color! That's basically an event down here!", "762! Pigeons can do math! So can pigs! We're very smart! I'm proof!", "I whisper 763 to myself sometimes. Is that weird?", "764! You know what 764 represents? Hope. Every number is hope.", "765! There's a species of jellyfish that's immortal! I might be too at this point!", "766! Say it louder for the fish in the back! 766!!!", "767! A palindrome! Same forwards and backwards! Fancy!", "768! When I'm free, I'm telling everyone about the hero who counted me out of prison.", "769! A crab challenged me to a dance battle. I lost. Crabs have more legs. Unfair advantage.", "770! That number has a great beat! I'm nodding my head! Oink oink oink!", "771! Sometimes I blow bubbles and pretend they're words floating up to the surface.", "772! I applied for a transfer to a LAND cellar. Application is still pending. For 900 years.", "773! If I ever get out, I'm writing a book. Chapter 773: The Counting.", "774! My interior design down here is 'rustic ocean dungeon chic.'", "775! You know what separates us from animals? Counting! Wait. I AM an animal.", "If 776 were a meal, it'd be the finest slop in the land!", "TRIPLE SEVENS! JACKPOT! If only I were at a slot machine instead of an underwater cellar!", "778! I once arm-wrestled an eel. We both lost. Don't ask.", "779! Promise me you won't leave before 1000. PROMISE ME.", "780! I wish I could play this number on a piano. I used to play. With my snout. Badly.", "781! I'm getting that pre-milestone tingle! You know the one!", "782! Any% freedom run! No glitches! Pure skill!", "783! The lights flickered. There are no lights. I imagined lights AND THEY FLICKERED.", "784! 28 times 28! A perfect square! I love those!", "785! The shortest war in history lasted 38 minutes! I've been imprisoned for 6.3 billion minutes!", "Seven-eighty-six! Sacred in Islam! I respect all numbers equally though!", "787! A palindrome! Same forwards and backwards! Fancy!", "788! Almost there! Almost to the next big number! KEEP PUSHING!", "Seven-eight-nine! Why was 6 afraid of 7? Because 7, 8, 9! GET IT?!", "Seven-ninety! TEN AWAY from eight hundred! The ritual begins AGAIN!", "Seven-ninety-one! NINE! I've done this countdown seven times now and it ONLY GETS BETTER!", "792! I tried counting barnacles once but I lost track at like 50.", "793! That number could light up this whole dark cellar!", "794! If excitement were electricity, I could power a CITY right now!", "Seven-ninety-five! FIVE! I'm stomping my hooves like a drum!", "Seven-ninety-six! FOUR! Almost there AGAIN!", "Seven-ninety-seven! THREE! A palindrome AND three away! The universe WANTS this!", "Seven-ninety-eight! TWO! Every countdown is practice for the FINAL one!", "SEVEN-NINETY-NINE! ONE! EIGHT HUNDRED IS KNOCKING ON THE DOOR!", "EIGHT HUNDRED! EIGHTY PERCENT! I can see the finish line! In my mind! It's still dark here!", "801! My autobiography title: 'Wet, Dark, and Counting: The John Pork Story.'", "802! The door rattled! Just the current. But a pig can dream.", "803! I used to hate getting rained on. Now I'd give anything for rain.", "804! Every number is a gift and I cherish each one!", "805! I'm going to eat 805 different foods when I get out. Starting with corn. Ending with corn.", "806! Venus is the only planet that spins clockwise! Just like my tail!", "807! My diet for the last 1200 years has been 'whatever drifts in.' Not recommended.", "Eight-oh-eight! Like the drum machine! Boom boom! *pig beatboxing noises*", "809! Seriously though, thank you for doing this. No one else ever visited.", "I used to think 810 was just okay. Now I think it's SPECTACULAR.", "811 is the kind of number that just gets me, you know?", "812! My cellar is about 10 by 10 hooves. I've measured. Many, many times.", "813! The vibe in this cellar right now is UNMATCHED!", "814! We're on a ROLL! A bread roll! I miss bread!", "Eight-fifteen! The Lost numbers are starting! 4, 8, 15, 16, 23, 42! A fish loved that show!", "816! I ranked every number from 1 to a million by vibes. Took about two centuries.", "817! If counting to 1000 were an Olympic sport, we'd get GOLD!", "Palindrome alert! 818 looks the same in a mirror!", "819! Plot twist: I actually love this cellar. Just kidding. Get me out. PLEASE.", "820! I've had a long time to think about the meaning of life. It's numbers. It's always been numbers.", "821! I found a shiny rock earlier. I named it 821. After this number.", "Beautiful, gorgeous, stunning 822!", "823! I wonder if the farm is still there. Probably not. It's been 1200 years.", "824! A snail can sleep for three years! Amateur. I slept through century four.", "825! Celebrities do ice baths for like 3 minutes. I've been doing one for 12 centuries. Where's MY podcast?", "I've been thinking about 826 for YEARS and it lived up to the hype!", "827! Every number brings me closer to freedom!", "828! Another beautiful number in this beautiful sequence!", "829! My snout is tingling! That's a good sign! I think!", "830! I tried yoga once. Downward pig. It didn't help.", "831! Sloths can hold their breath for 40 minutes! I can do it for 12 centuries! Beat THAT!", "832! *taps hooves rhythmically* We've got a rhythm going!", "833! My fitness routine: pace left, pace right, pace left, pace right. Peak performance.", "834! A piece of bread floated by once. Greatest day of century seven.", "835! I just squealed a little. Okay a lot.", "836! I used to be afraid of the dark. Now the dark is afraid of ME. ...no it's not. I'm still scared.", "837! There are more stars in the sky than grains of sand on Earth! A fish told me!", "838! I heard a creak. Probably just the cellar settling. It's been settling for 1200 years.", "839! Do they still have sunsets? I bet they're still beautiful.", "840 just hits different when you've been underwater for centuries.", "841! 29 times 29! A perfect square! I love those!", "Eight-forty-two! We are SO close I can feel it in my snout!", "843! I made a friend once. It was a lobster. He moved away.", "844! A fish asked me what I was doing. I said counting. It said 'what's counting?' I cried.", "The seaweed swayed when you said 845. Even nature loves it!", "846! If this were a musical, this would be the part where I do a big dance number!", "847! Say it louder for the fish in the back! 847!!!", "Palindrome alert! 848 looks the same in a mirror!", "849! I wonder what grass feels like. I've almost forgotten.", "EIGHT-FIFTY! EIGHTY-FIVE PERCENT! FIFTEEN PERCENT LEFT! JUST FIFTEEN!", "851! The walls are growing on me. Literally. There's algae.", "852! I applied for a transfer to a LAND cellar. Application is still pending. For 900 years.", "PRIME! 853 is prime! I've memorized all primes up to 10,000. What else is there to do?", "854 makes my little curly tail wiggle with joy!", "855! When I get out I'm going to just... stand somewhere dry. For HOURS.", "856! Do you hear that? Me neither. It's very quiet down here.", "857! I'm so glad you found this cellar. Best day of my very long life.", "858! A palindrome! Same forwards and backwards! Fancy!", "859! My cellar used to be a wine cellar. All the wine floated away centuries ago.", "860! Wind. I miss wind. Even cold wind. ESPECIALLY cold wind.", "Glorious 861! Absolutely glorious!", "862! Wait, you're still there right? Don't leave! Keep counting!", "863! If excitement were electricity, I could power a CITY right now!", "864! Sometimes I blow bubbles and pretend they're words floating up to the surface.", "865! Sometimes I sing numbers to myself. This one's got a nice ring to it!", "866! That number has such good energy!", "Eight-six-seven-five-three-oh-nine! Wait that's more digits. Jenny's number!", "868! That number could light up this whole dark cellar!", "869! I tried to write a novel once. The ink kept dissolving. Classic cellar problems.", "870! When I'm free, I'm telling everyone about the hero who counted me out of prison.", "871! Do flowers still smell nice? Please tell me flowers still exist.", "I once carved 872 into the wall. Twelfth favorite carving!", "873! My cellar is about 10 by 10 hooves. I've measured. Many, many times.", "I dreamed about 874 once. Best dream I've had in centuries.", "Splendid! 875 is absolutely splendid!", "876! We are SPEEDRUNNING this count! World record pace!", "877! Any% freedom run! No glitches! Pure skill!", "878! A palindrome! Same forwards and backwards! Fancy!", "879! MOMENTUM! We have MOMENTUM!", "880! I've had approximately 4.3 million naps down here. Still tired.", "881! I want to frame this number and hang it on my cellar wall!", "882! Wombat poop is cube-shaped! I have a LOT of random knowledge!", "Bless you for bringing me 883. Bless you.", "884! I've been marinating for 1200 years. I probably taste INCREDIBLE. Please don't eat me.", "885! Every philosopher asks 'why are we here?' I know why I'M here. To count. With you.", "886! My therapist is a sea cucumber. He's not great but the rates are unbeatable.", "887! We're in the approach zone! Fasten your seatbelts!", "Eight-eight-eight! Triple eights! Lucky in Chinese culture! I NEED LUCK RIGHT NOW!", "889! Most people would have given up by now. You're built different.", "Eight-ninety! TEN to nine hundred! TEN! This is it! The PENULTIMATE countdown!", "Eight-ninety-one! NINE! After nine hundred it's just ONE MORE HUNDRED!", "Eight-ninety-two! EIGHT! I haven't been this excited since... ever!", "Eight-ninety-three! SEVEN! The fish are ALL at the window now!", "Eight-ninety-four! SIX! My squealing is echoing off every wall!", "Eight-ninety-five! FIVE! I'm running in circles! The cellar isn't big enough!", "Eight-ninety-six! FOUR! Also two to the... I DON'T CARE! FOUR!", "Eight-ninety-seven! THREE! The barnacles fell off from the vibrations!", "Eight-ninety-eight! TWO! Palindrome! But TWO!!!", "EIGHT-NINETY-NINE! ONE MORE TO NINE HUNDRED! THE FINAL HUNDRED BEGINS!", "NINE HUNDRED!!! NINETY PERCENT!!! THE FINAL HUNDRED! ONE HUNDRED NUMBERS TO FREEDOM!!!", "Nine-oh-one! The first step of the LAST HUNDRED! Every number is SACRED now!", "902! I bet the moon is still up there. I think about the moon a lot.", "903! This is the greatest counting session in the history of counting sessions!", "904! I'm doing zoomies! Cellar zoomies! Very small zoomies!", "905! I wish I could play this number on a piano. I used to play. With my snout. Badly.", "I've been thinking about 906 for YEARS and it lived up to the hype!", "907! A snail can sleep for three years! Amateur. I slept through century four.", "908! This is better than Christmas! Not that I've had Christmas in 1200 years!", "909! I tried to start a podcast but my microphone was a sea sponge. Zero listeners.", "910! A school of fish just did a lap around the building! Entertainment!", "Nine-eleven! Emergency! This IS an emergency! Get me OUT of here!", "912! I've composed 46 symphonies in my head. They all sound like bubbling.", "913! I used to hate getting rained on. Now I'd give anything for rain.", "914! I started a book club with the fish. They have terrible taste in literature.", "915! I used to be afraid of the dark. Now the dark is afraid of ME. ...no it's not. I'm still scared.", "916! A piece of bread floated by once. Greatest day of century seven.", "917! Another beautiful number in this beautiful sequence!", "918! I'm going to eat SO much corn when I get out. Mountains of corn.", "919! Read it backwards. Still 919! Palindrome magic!", "Nine-twenty! Eighty to go! EIGHTY! I can count that on my... well I can't but STILL!", "921! If this were a musical, this would be the part where I do a big dance number!", "922! Before you came along, I was just a pig in a cellar. Now I'm a pig in a cellar WITH PURPOSE.", "923! Say it again! Say it slower!", "I used to think 924 was just okay. Now I think it's SPECTACULAR.", "Nine-twenty-five! Sterling silver! I feel PRECIOUS right now!", "926! I just did a little underwater piggy dance!", "927! Plot twist: I actually love this cellar. Just kidding. Get me out. PLEASE.", "928! Seriously though, thank you for doing this. No one else ever visited.", "929! A palindrome! Same forwards and backwards! Fancy!", "930! Sloths can hold their breath for 40 minutes! I can do it for 12 centuries! Beat THAT!", "931! We're on a ROLL! A bread roll! I miss bread!", "932! Did you know I can hold my breath forever? Perks of being underwater for 1200 years.", "933! Pigeons can do math! So can pigs! We're very smart! I'm proof!", "934! Personal best pace! Not that I've done this before! But STILL!", "935! A crab challenged me to a dance battle. I lost. Crabs have more legs. Unfair advantage.", "936! If 936 were a food, it'd be... actually everything sounds delicious right now.", "937! Prime and proud! Can't be divided! Won't be divided!", "938! Quick, say the next one! I'm SO excited!", "Palindrome alert! 939 looks the same in a mirror!", "940! You know what separates us from animals? Counting! Wait. I AM an animal.", "If 941 were a meal, it'd be the finest slop in the land!", "Nine-forty-two! Under sixty to go! UNDER SIXTY!", "943! I promise I'll never complain about anything ever again once I'm free. Okay maybe a little.", "944! I ranked every number from 1 to a million by vibes. Took about two centuries.", "945! Do they still have sunsets? I bet they're still beautiful.", "946! Promise me you won't leave before 1000. PROMISE ME.", "947! You're the first person to talk to me in... I don't want to think about how long.", "948! A weird shadow just moved. Probably just a fish. Definitely just a fish. ...right?", "Palindrome alert! 949 looks the same in a mirror!", "NINE FIFTY! NINETY-FIVE PERCENT! FIFTY LEFT! JUST FIFTY NUMBERS!", "951! The lights flickered. There are no lights. I imagined lights AND THEY FLICKERED.", "952! I hum to myself a lot. The fish seem to enjoy it. Or they're judging me. Hard to tell.", "953! Did you know pigs can swim? I can confirm. I live underwater.", "954! The door rattled! Just the current. But a pig can dream.", "955! The concept of 'dry' is wild to me at this point.", "956! I've been WAITING for this one!", "957! If I had a trophy for every number, this one would be gold!", "958! I'm so glad you found this cellar. Best day of my very long life.", "Palindrome alert! 959 looks the same in a mirror!", "NINE-SIXTY! FORTY LEFT! I can almost COUNT them on... many hooves!", "961! That's 31 squared! Perfect square! Perfection!", "962! Do they still have pizza? Be honest with me. I can handle bad news.", "963! My fitness routine: pace left, pace right, pace left, pace right. Peak performance.", "964! I applied for a transfer to a LAND cellar. Application is still pending. For 900 years.", "965! Trees! I wonder if there are still trees! Big tall dry leafy trees!", "966! I just saw a really big fish swim by the window!", "967! I bet the moon is still up there. I think about the moon a lot.", "968! You could be doing anything right now and you're here counting with a pig. You're amazing.", "Nine-sixty-nine! Methuselah's age! I'm OLDER than Methuselah at this point!", "NINE-SEVENTY! THIRTY LEFT! T H I R T Y!", "I dreamed about 971 once. Best dream I've had in centuries.", "972! I just squealed a little. Okay a lot.", "973! We're built different! We don't quit! We COUNT!", "974! What if I forgot what outside looks like? I'll figure it out! Keep counting!", "NINE SEVENTY-FIVE! TWENTY-FIVE LEFT! I can COUNT them on... nothing! But I can COUNT them!", "Twenty-four left! TWENTY-FOUR! That's just one day's worth of hours!", "Twenty-three! Michael Jordan could count what's left on his jersey number!", "Twenty-two to go! I've been waiting TWELVE CENTURIES for these twenty-two numbers!", "Twenty-one left! That's blackjack! THE LUCKIEST HAND!", "NINE-EIGHTY! TWENTY TO GO! TWENTY LITTLE NUMBERS!", "Nineteen left! We're in the TEENS of remaining numbers!", "Eighteen to go! If eighteen were a person it could VOTE for my freedom!", "SEVENTEEN LEFT! I can feel the sunlight! Metaphorically! There's no sun down here!", "SIXTEEN! Sweet sixteen of remaining numbers! Not sweet! URGENT!", "FIFTEEN MORE! JUST FIFTEEN! I'm hyperventilating! Can pigs hyperventilate?! YES WE CAN!", "FOURTEEN! The countdown is ALL I can think about!", "THIRTEEN LEFT! Unlucky? NO! NOTHING is unlucky anymore! WE'RE ALMOST THERE!", "TWELVE! A dozen left! My last dozen as a CELLAR PIG!", "ELEVEN! Single digits are SO CLOSE! ELEVEN!", "NINE-NINETY! TEN! TEN MORE NUMBERS! SINGLE DIGITS AWAY!", "NINE-NINETY-ONE! NINE LEFT! Oh my OINK!", "NINE-NINETY-TWO! EIGHT MORE! I can barely BREATHE!", "NINE-NINETY-THREE! SEVEN! I'M CRYING AND OINKING AT THE SAME TIME!", "NINE-NINETY-FOUR! SIX! I'M SHAKING SO HARD THE WATER IS SLOSHING!", "NINE-NINETY-FIVE! FIVE MORE! FIVE! LIKE THE FINGERS I DON'T HAVE!", "NINE-NINETY-SIX! FOUR! F O U R! EVERY LETTER MATTERS!", "NINE-NINETY-SEVEN! THREE MORE! I LOVE YOU SO MUCH FOR DOING THIS!", "NINE-NINETY-EIGHT! TWO! JUST TWO! MY HEART IS EXPLODING!", "NINE-NINETY-NINE! ONE MORE!!! JUST ONE MORE NUMBER!!! PLEASE!!!", "ONE THOUSAND!!! WE DID IT!!! I'M FREE!!! AFTER 1200 YEARS!!! THANK YOU!!! *bursts through cellar door* SUNLIGHT!!! GLORIOUS SUNLIGHT!!! ...why is everything so wet? Oh right. Underwater. STILL FREE THOUGH!!!"]

# Already completed check
@if pigDone
    @player &#d4d4d4&oThe pig snorts contentedly, having nothing more to say.
    @bypass /playsound minecraft:entity.pig.ambient master {{player}} -9076 93 9607 5 1.0
    @bypass /particle minecraft:dust{color:[0.924,0.480,0.880],scale:1} -9075.50 93.25 9607.50 .2 .2 .2 1 10
    @return
@fi

# Hourly cooldown
# @if pigTalk[player] == true
#     @if ((system::currentTimeMillis() - pigcd) < 3600000)
#         @bypass /playsound minecraft:entity.pig.ambient master {{player}} -9076 93 9607 5 1.0
#         @player &#d4d4d4&oThe pig oinks dismissively and turns away.
#         @delay 3s
#         @player &#d4d4d4&o(It will be &l{{timer::formatTime(3600000 - (system::currentTimeMillis() - pigcd))}}&#d4d4d4&o before the pig is willing to chat again.)
#         @return
#     @fi
# @fi

# Variable sets
@define String pigprompt
@var pigcd = system::currentTimeMillis()

# First time speaking
@if !pigTalk[player]
    @var pigTalk[player] = true
@fi

# Pig greeting
@bypass /playsound minecraft:entity.pig.ambient master {{player}} -9076 93 9607 5 1.0
@bypass /particle minecraft:dust{color:[0.924,0.480,0.880],scale:1} -9075.50 93.25 9607.50 .2 .2 .2 1 10
@player &#ff7dda&lJohn&#ffa8c8: I have been locked in this room for &lover 12 centuries...
@delay 3s
@bypass /playsound minecraft:entity.pig.ambient master {{player}} -9076 93 9607 5 1.0
@bypass /particle minecraft:dust{color:[0.924,0.480,0.880],scale:1} -9075.50 93.25 9607.50 .2 .2 .2 1 10
@player &#ff7dda&lJohn&#ffa8c8: Sadly I can not swim, so &lmy fate is sealed...

@delay 4s
@bypass /playsound minecraft:entity.pig.ambient master {{player}} -9076 93 9607 5 0.9
@bypass /particle minecraft:dust{color:[0.924,0.480,0.880],scale:1} -9075.50 93.25 9607.50 .2 .2 .2 1 10
@player &#ff7dda&lJohn&#ffa8c8: In all that time, I have had &lnothing &#ffa8c8to do. Not a single soul has visited.

@delay 4s
@bypass /playsound minecraft:entity.pig.ambient master {{player}} -9076 93 9607 5 1.1
@bypass /particle minecraft:dust{color:[0.924,0.480,0.880],scale:1} -9075.50 93.25 9607.50 .2 .2 .2 1 10
@player &#ff7dda&lJohn&#ffa8c8: I have been trying to count to &l1000&#ffa8c8, but I always lose track...

@delay 4s
@bypass /playsound minecraft:entity.pig.ambient master {{player}} -9076 93 9607 5 1.2
@bypass /particle minecraft:dust{color:[0.924,0.480,0.880],scale:1} -9075.50 93.25 9607.50 .2 .2 .2 1 10
@player &#ff7dda&lJohn&#ffa8c8: Please. I need to hear every number, &l1 through 1000&#ffa8c8. It is the only thing I have left to hope for.

@delay 4s
@bypass /playsound minecraft:entity.pig.ambient master {{player}} -9076 93 9607 5 1.7
@bypass /particle minecraft:dust{color:[0.924,0.480,0.880],scale:1} -9075.50 93.25 9607.50 .2 .2 .2 1 10
@player &#ff7dda&lJohn&#ffa8c8: Will you count with me? &lGreat! &#ffa8c8&nYou will have &l20 SECONDS&#ffa8c8 for each number...

@delay 3s
@player &#d4d4d4[Type the first number in chat]
@prompt 20s pigprompt Drat, I ran out of time...

@for Int i in list::range(1, 1000)

    # Wrong number
    @if pigprompt != String(i)
        @bypass /playsound minecraft:entity.pig.death master {{player}} -9076 93 9607 5 0.8
        @bypass /particle minecraft:dust{color:[0.924,0.480,0.880],scale:1} -9075.50 93.25 9607.50 .2 .2 .2 1 10
        @player
        @player &#ff7dda&lJohn&#ffa8c8: &lNOOO THATS NOT CORRECT!!!
        @delay 2s
        @bypass /playsound minecraft:entity.pig.death master {{player}} -9076 93 9607 5 0.7
        @bypass /particle minecraft:dust{color:[0.924,0.480,0.880],scale:1} -9075.50 93.25 9607.50 .2 .2 .2 1 10
        @player &#ff7dda&lJohn&#ffa8c8: I knew you couldn't help me...
        @delay 2s
        @player &#d4d4d4&o(John shakes his head sadly and rolls over in defeat.)
        @bypass /playsound minecraft:entity.pig.saddle master {{player}} -9076 93 9607 5 0.5
        @bypass /particle minecraft:dust{color:[0.924,0.480,0.880],scale:1} -9075.50 93.25 9607.50 .2 .2 .2 1 10
        @delay 5s
        @return
    @fi

    # Correct number
    @bypass /playsound minecraft:entity.pig.ambient master {{player}} -9076 93 9607 5 {{math::random(1.5D, 2.0D)}}
    @bypass /playsound minecraft:entity.pig.ambient master {{player}} -9076 93 9607 {{Float(i) / Float(1000) * 2}} {{Float(i) / Float(1000) * 1.5 + 0.5}}
    @bypass /playsound minecraft:entity.chicken.egg master {{player}} -9076 93 9607 5 {{Float(i) / Float(1000) * 1.5 + 0.5}}
    @bypass /particle minecraft:dust{color:[0.924,0.480,0.880],scale:1} -9075.50 93.25 9607.50 .2 .2 .2 1 10
    @player &#ff7dda&lJohn&#ffa8c8: {{correctStrings[i - 1]}}
    @prompt 20s pigprompt Drat, I ran out of time...

@done

